{
	title: 'Terminal output and redraw',
	spec: "Items in the transcript are separated by exactly one blank row: trailing whitespace and newlines the model streamed at the end of a text or thinking block are not drawn, so [paused] after a cut-off answer has one blank row before it. Render transcript, streaming answer and prompt like a normal REPL: start at the current cursor without clearing, and leave the last frame visible on quit, suspend and restart, all but its last row (the help row): that row is erased and the cursor left at its start, so the shell prompt or the restarted Hal takes it and nothing scrolls. When the frame first outgrows the terminal height, switch one-way to fullscreen mode per the terminal.md artifact (grow and full modes, never slice history to the viewport, scrollback is immutable). One tested width helper handles wide and combining characters and wrapping. Restore terminal mode on exit or crash. Test with a fake terminal. Lift the strings.ts artifact (width and wrapping) and its tests. A word wider than its row (a URL, an OAuth link) is never broken by the wrapper: it gets a row of its own that flows on at the full terminal width, first terminal row after the left pad, the rest from column 0, with no pad or fill inside it, written without CRLF between so the terminal soft-wraps it into one line that opens and copies whole; a change anywhere in such a chain rewrites it whole from its first row. Table cells and tool-output glimpses still break long words. Output never holds the event loop (task 7j): the real terminal's writes queue and go out in order by async fs.write on the thread pool, 64 KiB at a time (terminal.writer), so a slow terminal never blocks a synchronous write for as long as it takes to read megabytes; a frame painted while a big one is going out waits behind it, so the screen is never corrupted. A full repaint's rows are joined 1,000 at a time as the writer reaches them (Output.defer), not all at once. On every way out (exit, suspend, leaving raw mode) the queue is flushed synchronously.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The artifact\'s wordWrap had bugs: it kept the breaking space ("the quick "), and it measured tabs from the start of the source line, not of the wrapped row, so a tab could make a row too wide. The src version measures columns per row and tests widths as an invariant over many widths; keep that test when touching wrapping.',
		'frame.clean() must keep UTF-16 offsets unchanged (no CRLF folding there), because the prompt cursor is an offset into the raw text. Line-ending normalization happens only in wrap(), for display text.',
		"Bun emits 'exit' on uncaught errors and rejections, but not on SIGTERM/SIGHUP; realIO installs handlers that call process.exit so the restore runs. A new exit path must go through 'exit' or leave().",
		'A forced grow-mode repaint is only safe while our top is still on screen. If the terminal got shorter than cursorRow, render switches to full mode rather than leaving stale rows above.',
		'Shrink bugs hide: a one-row fullscreen shrink repainted in place happens to look right. The test shrinks the prompt by two rows and then edits every row; keep tests at that strength.',
		'Every frame line is at most one terminal row, so frame rows equal terminal rows. Long words (URLs) soft-wrap without physical-row bookkeeping (lineTops): paintRows splits them into rows ending in ansi.FLOW, an APC the renderer strips. Tool-output glimpses keep hard breaks, as they count rows and a minified line could be megabytes.',
		"render.test.ts has a small terminal emulator (scrollback, clamped cursor moves, CSI J/K/G/H/3J). Reuse it for later terminal work; it throws on sequences it doesn't know, which catches accidental ones.",
		'terminal.writer: process.stdout.write to a tty is synchronous in Bun and blocks until the terminal has read it all (a 4 MB write to a slow reader held the loop for seconds); fs.write(1, ...) runs on the thread pool and does not. flush() at exit cannot wait for the chunk already handed to fs.write, so quitting mid-repaint may put the restore sequence before or inside that last chunk; the next paint or shell prompt recovers.',
		"Bug fixed: park wrote CRLF below the frame, so a full-screen frame scrolled up one row on quit and the restarted Hal's repaint visibly jumped. Invariant: leaving the terminal never scrolls; park erases the frame's last row (CSI 2K) and parks the cursor there.",
		"Bug fixed: Hal's hand-made wide-glyph table predated Unicode 16, so U+2630 (☰, which models write for the web menu) measured 1 column while terminals draw 2; a notice overlaid on such a row overflowed, wrapped, and desynced the renderer's rows while streaming. Invariant: charWidth agrees with the terminal's Unicode tables; it delegates non-ASCII code points to Bun.stringWidth (also faster than the table), keeping our zero-width set, tab stops, cluster joining and the Ghostty-matched VS16 rule (text symbols stay narrow; VS16 after an astral emoji makes it wide)."
	],
	needs: ['11', 'ca']
}
